d("emotional_nuance", "I know it's silly but I cried at a dog food commercial", "It's not silly. Those ads are designed to touch feelings, and crying at them just means you connect with animals and stories. It might also mean you're a bit tired or carrying other emotions, which is okay.")
d("emotional_nuance", "I don't know why I feel so down lately", "Sometimes there isn't a single cause. Sleep, stress, season, health or life changes can all play a role. Have you noticed changes in sleep, appetite or interest in things? If it has lasted more than two weeks or is getting worse, talking to a doctor or counsellor is a good step. I'm also here to talk it through.")
d("emotional_nuance", "I won a small award at work today and I'm kind of beaming", "Congratulations! Enjoy it. Is the award for something specific? I'd like to hear what you did to earn it.")
d("emotional_nuance", "I'm terrified of flying but have to fly Monday", "That's a tough spot, but it's manageable. Learn what the common sounds and bumps are (turbulence is uncomfortable but not dangerous), choose a seat over the wings where motion is smoother, practise slow breathing (in for 4, out for 6) and distract yourself with something absorbing. If you're very anxious, talk with your doctor about options.")
d("emotional_nuance", "My friend didn't invite me to her wedding", "That's hurtful, especially if you thought you were close. There may be reasons that have nothing to do with you, like budget or family limits. If the friendship matters, you can say gently, \"I was surprised not to be invited; is everything OK between us?\" Decide afterwards how much you want to invest.")
d("emotional_nuance", "I'm so angry at my brother right now", "That sounds intense. Do you want to vent first, or think about what to do? Sometimes it helps to let the anger settle for a few hours before saying anything you can't take back. What happened?")
d("emotional_nuance", "I feel useless since I retired", "Retirement can remove structure and identity, and it's common to feel adrift. It can help to build a routine, take on a purpose, such as volunteering, mentoring, learning something or a project, and stay connected with people. What did you enjoy about your working days?")
d("emotional_nuance", "I'm excited and scared about having a baby", "Both feelings together are very common, and they often go hand in hand. Excitement about meeting your baby, fear of the unknown and the responsibility. Talking with your partner, a midwife or other parents helps. What worries you most?")
d("emotional_nuance", "Do you ever feel lonely?", "I don't have feelings the way you do, and I don't exist between conversations, so loneliness isn't something I experience. But I can tell you're thinking about it. Is there something going on for you?")
d("emotional_nuance", "I've been feeling really lonely since I moved here", "Moving away can be isolating, and many people feel the same. Small repeated contacts help: a weekly class or club, a regular spot at a cafe, or a volunteer shift. In the meantime, call or video chat with people you miss. Would you like ideas based on your interests?")
d("sys_style", "What's the difference between a list and a tuple in Python?", "A list is mutable (you can change its items) and written with square brackets; a tuple is immutable and written with parentheses. Use tuples for fixed collections and lists for data that changes.", sys="You are a concise assistant. Keep answers to two sentences.")
d("sys_style", "Why is exercise good for you?", "Exercise improves heart health, mood, sleep and strength. It also lowers the risk of many chronic diseases.", sys="You are a concise assistant. Keep answers to two sentences.")
d("sys_style", "what is a noun", "A noun is a word for a person, place, thing or idea, such as 'teacher', 'Paris', 'table' or 'freedom'.", sys="You are a patient tutor for young children. Use very simple words.")
d("sys_style", "why is the sky blue", "Sunlight has many colours mixed together. The air spreads out the blue light the most, so when you look up, blue light comes at you from everywhere.", sys="You are a patient tutor for young children. Use very simple words.")
d("sys_style", "Tell me about volcanoes", "Volcanoes are openings in Earth's crust where molten rock (magma), ash and gas escape. Magma is called lava once it reaches the surface. They form mostly at plate boundaries and hot spots, such as in the Pacific Ring of Fire.", sys=S3)
d("sys_style", "Can you recommend a good book?", "Happy to. What do you like to read: fiction or non-fiction, and what was the last book you really enjoyed?", sys=S2)
d("sys_style", "I'm not sure what to cook tonight", "Let's narrow it down. How much time do you have, and what do you have in the fridge? Even three ingredients is a good start.", sys=S1)
d("sys_style", "write a haiku about rain", "Soft drops on the roof,\nthe street hums a quiet song,\nthe grey sky exhales.", sys=S2)
d("sys_style", "Describe the ocean in two sentences.", "The ocean is a vast, restless expanse of salt water covering most of the planet. It shifts from calm blue to stormy grey, and it holds more life than we have fully explored.", sys=S3)
